WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.250
I do want to talk before we move on about
just the sort of addendum story to the entire,

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.289
uh, Ukraine impeachment fiasco, Joe Biden
scandal.

00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:15.459
This is sort of an ancillary story, but it
is part of the continuing comedy of errors

00:00:15.459 --> 00:00:20.449
that the white, uh, that the Trump white house
continues to be the Trump white house accidentally

00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:27.619
set their talking points on the Ukraine fiasco
directly to house Democrats and Nancy Pelosi.

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:32.610
And every time that I see a new headline about
the entire Ukraine fiasco, I think this one

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.160
has to be wrong.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.500
This one must be from a satirical news website
or something, but the headlines are real.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.239
There were talking points that the Republicans
put together the Trump white house and with

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:48.969
Republicans put together to fight against
house Democrats who of course have essentially

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:52.140
launched an impeachment inquiry against Donald
Trump.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.640
And they put those documents together, they
put those talking points together and then

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.219
they send them directly to Democrats.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:02.390
And this is the funniest thing, but after
we do this, I want to talk about the content

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:03.830
of the talking points themselves.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:09.190
So they send out, uh, the, the talking points
and it contains a defense of the phone call

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.980
between Trump and the Ukrainian president.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:11.980
Why?

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.090
It was all great, how the real scandal is
the leak, about the content of the phone call,

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.440
not the content of the phone call itself.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:25.180
And then shortly thereafter, the white house
realizing its mistake, tries to recall the

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:30.070
message through their email system, which
of course it was too late to do as the ship

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.070
had sailed.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.930
And the talking points had been published
or work to be published soon thereafter.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.810
So more in competence at the Trump white house.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.680
But the content of the talking points is actually
the most important thing here.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:49.200
You can tell how weak the hand of Republicans
is by their talking points.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.180
For example, their defense of the allegation
that there is a quid pro quo between Donald

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.490
Trump's military aid and Ukraine smearing
Biden.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.360
Their talking point is that the aid package
wasn't specifically mentioned in the call.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:10.369
And as we've since found out, the phone call
had as a precondition this desire to talk

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:14.340
about Joe Biden and the investigation and
the eventual smear that they hope it would

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.340
come.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.370
Anyone who knows anything about politics knows
that this is not how things work.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:25.099
Trump doesn't personally on the same call,
uh, ask for an investigation into Biden and

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:27.909
say, until you do it, I'm not giving you the
money.

00:02:27.909 --> 00:02:29.439
This is not how politics works.

00:02:29.439 --> 00:02:31.010
This is not how quid pro quo works.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:34.489
This is not how ultimatums work and holding
hostage of military aid.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:38.939
And of course we've since found out that there
was already a discussion in advance and Rudy

00:02:38.939 --> 00:02:43.110
Giuliani was involved and other people were
involved in setting the preconditions for

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:47.210
this phone call between Trump and the Ukrainian
president to even take place.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:51.849
These talking points that they sent out as
boneheaded as it is to send it directly to

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:59.819
Democrats are talking points that would only
even possibly work on the most naive and uninformed

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:01.400
follower of politics.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.709
You can tell how weak their talking points
are because they mentioned the deep state

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:08.250
in their talking points.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:15.120
They say as a suggested talking point that
this case just shows another example of the

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.639
